<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sanjakbey</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as sancakbeys</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A sanjakbey (sancakbey) was the governor of a sanjak, a district-level province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. Sanjakbeys held military and administrative authority, commanded the local timariot cavalry and answered to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylerbey">beylerbeys</a> who governed larger provinces. Accounts of the Ottoman Empire describe this hierarchy of governors as the means by which imperial authority was extended across a vast territory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sanjakbey.jpg" alt="Sanjakbey" width="272" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1586 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Secaatname_0057._Asafi_Pasha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
